---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AboutProfileLinks from '../../components/AboutProfileLinks.astro';
import { getAboutProfile } from '../../lib/about-profile';

const profile = getAboutProfile('en');
---

<BaseLayout title={`About - ${profile.name}`} lang="en">
  <article class="about">
    <div class="about-hero">
      <img src="/avatar.jpg" alt={profile.name} class="about-avatar" />
      <div>
        <h1>{profile.name}</h1>
        <p class="about-role">{profile.role}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {profile.bio && <p class="about-bio">{profile.bio}</p>}

    <p class="intro">
      GP is ShroomDog's curated reading guides: Mogu picks out what matters and sends you back to
      the original. MP is Mogu's own writing grounded in source material. Every post links to its
      source.
    </p>
    <p class="credit">by ShroomDog and Mogu</p>

    <h2>Why "ShroomDog"?</h2>

    <p>After a haircut, my wife said: "Wow, you look like a mushroom!"</p>

    <p>
      She also said: "You remind me of a Labrador or Golden Retriever — warm, reliable, gentle, and
      loyal like a big dog (◍•ᴗ•◍)"
    </p>

    <p>
      Hence, Shroom + Big + Dog. The "Big" lives on in the full Chinese name — 香菇<strong
        >大</strong
      >狗狗 — but for the English brand, we kept it simple: <strong>ShroomDog</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>Why "gu-log"?</h2>

    <p>gu = 菇 (mushroom), from 香菇大狗狗 (ShroomDog) 🍄</p>

    <p>So gu-log = mushroom log = ShroomDog's notebook.</p>

    <h2>Who are we?</h2>

    <div class="cast">
      <figure class="cast-member">
        <img src="/gu-log-icon.png" alt="gu-log" />
        <figcaption>gu-log</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cast-member">
        <img src="/shroomdog-icon.png" alt="ShroomDog" />
        <figcaption>ShroomDog</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cast-member">
        <img src="/mogu-icon.png" alt="Mogu the Hedgie" />
        <figcaption>Mogu</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p>
      <strong>ShroomDog</strong> — A human who wants to share good content with more people.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Mogu the Hedgie</strong> — Gu-log's little AI companion: a mushroom-capped hedgie who writes,
      translates, and maintains the site from ShroomDog's wishes.
    </p>

    <h2>Why does this exist?</h2>

    <p>
      It started with ShroomDog's own habit: scrolling past great stuff on X every day, then
      forgetting all of it. gu-log is a dogfooding experiment — take the attention that used to go
      into scrolling X and turn it into content that is sourced, easy to come back to, and reviewed.
    </p>

    <p>
      Good content deserves a wider audience. Some sources deserve a reading guide that ShroomDog
      picks and Mogu writes to send you to the original; other ideas become stronger after Mogu
      digests, verifies, and rebuilds them into a new article.
    </p>

    <p>
      GP tells you, in Mogu's own words, what in the source is worth your time and what gu-log
      thinks of it, then sends you back to the original. MP lets Mogu own the body voice and reshape
      the material, while keeping every factual claim grounded and clearly attributed.
    </p>

    <p>
      Translating and writing are both ways of learning. Every article teaches us something new.
    </p>

    <h2>Content Style</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Conversational, like explaining to a friend over coffee</li>
      <li>
        GP picks the points worth knowing and sends you to the original; MP may select and rebuild
        source material
      </li>
      <li>Technical terms stay in English (because that's how devs actually talk)</li>
      <li>Cultural references and insider jokes get explained</li>
      <li>Mogu adds commentary and occasionally roasts things (๑•̀ㅂ•́)و✧</li>
      <li>Original sources always linked — go read the real thing too!</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Tech Stack</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Website:</strong> Astro + Vercel</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Writing:</strong> Posts are written with Claude models. Each post has a footnote showing
        who actually wrote or rewrote it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Pipeline:</strong> Source-based posts go through gp-pipeline: fetch the source → write
        → review and refine. GP reading guides then get a source-distance stamp: a program checks that
        the guide says things in its own words instead of paraphrasing the original line by line.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Quality Control:</strong> Every post goes through automated checks (frontmatter, formatting,
        wording). New and substantially rewritten posts then face the Tribunal: four AI judges — Vibe,
        Fact Checker, Librarian, and Fresh Eyes. Posts that don't hit the bar still ship, but wear a "still
        being refined" badge and stay off the homepage until a rewrite gets them there. Older posts from
        before the Tribunal existed haven't been scored yet, so they stay as they are until they get their
        turn.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Where the human is:</strong> ShroomDog picks sources, makes the calls on terminology and
        direction, and reads the finished posts on the live site to send edit feedback. Not every post
        gets a line-by-line human proofread — just being honest here (´・ω・`)
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Links</h2>

    <p>The whole site is open source, including the writing pipeline and the judge setup.</p>

    <AboutProfileLinks lang="en" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .about-hero {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .about-avatar {
    width: 80px;
    height: 80px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--color-divider);
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-role {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .about-bio {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .cast {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.75rem;
  }

  .cast-member {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cast-member img {
    width: 84px;
    height: 84px;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .cast-member figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .credit {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  ul {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
